---
# Scrutiny's time-series store. scrutiny-web is the only client: it reads
# SCRUTINY_WEB_INFLUXDB_HOST / _PORT=8086 (web.yaml.j2). The collector DaemonSet does NOT write
# here — it posts to scrutiny-web's API, which does the InfluxDB writes.
#
# THIS POLICY SHIPS WITH THE ROLE THAT NEEDS IT. It lived in roles/k8s/netpol-baseline/ until
# 2026-09-10, one role away from the Deployment whose startup depends on it (#1620, the same
# split as authelia's session store in #1609). scrutiny-web EXITS rather than degrades when
# InfluxDB is unreachable: it calls `/api/v2/setup` during AppEngine.Setup and `panic(err)`s on
# a connection error instead of retrying (upstream
# webapp/backend/pkg/web/middleware/repository.go, read against upstream master 2026-09-06 —
# see web.yaml.j2's `wait-for-influxdb` comment). That gate is bounded at 60 x 2s, so with this
# policy absent the pod fails init after two minutes and backs off. `build_k8s_dep_map` cannot
# see a split like it — it derives a role's edges from templates inside that role's own
# directory (ansible/filter_plugins/toposort.py), so a dependency expressed in a sibling role
# produces no edge and no ordering constraint to violate.
# ansible/tests/services/test_scrutiny_influxdb_policy.py pins the co-location.
#
# 8086 is the containerPort AND the Service port — verified 2026-08-20, they match, and that
# same test keeps them matching.
#
# NO `netpol_baseline_enforced` BRANCH, unlike netpol-baseline's own policies. That lever is a
# role default of netpol-baseline, and Ansible role defaults are role-scoped: it does not
# resolve here, and `| default(true)` would read as honouring the lever while ignoring it.
# Dropping it is also the right behaviour rather than a concession — the lever exists to
# restore reachability in a rollback, and the only path that reaches InfluxDB at all is the one
# this file grants, so leaving it on cannot be what an operator is rolling back from.
apiVersion: networking.k8s.io/v1
kind: NetworkPolicy
metadata:
  name: scrutiny-influxdb
  namespace: {{ k8s_namespace }}
spec:
  podSelector:
    matchLabels:
      app: scrutiny-influxdb
  policyTypes:
    - Ingress
  ingress:
    - from:
        - podSelector:
            matchLabels:
              app: scrutiny-web
      ports:
        - port: 8086
          protocol: TCP
